<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 20 March, from 1602 to 1933.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1602">1602 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">424 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dutch East India Company is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The States General granted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">VOC</a> a monopoly on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. Financed by publicly traded shares, it could wage war, make treaties and found colonies, and dominated the spice trade.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1724">1724 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">302 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A papal conclave opens in Rome after Innocent XIII's death</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>, largely the same as those who had chosen Pope Innocent XIII in 1721, met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> to elect his successor. On 28 May they elected Cardinal Pierfrancesco Orsini, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican friar</a>, as Pope Benedict XIII.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon returns to Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xviii">Louis XVIII</a> fled, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> entered the Tuileries to cheering crowds. His restored rule, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a>, ended with defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> in June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1852">1852 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">174 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Harriet Beecher Stowe publishes 'Uncle Tom's Cabin'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stowe's novel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> sold some 300,000 copies in America in its first year and stirred anti-slavery feeling in the North. Lincoln is said to have greeted her as the author who started the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1854">1854 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">172 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Opponents of slavery meet at Ripon to form a new party</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting in a schoolhouse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ripon">Ripon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a>, opponents of the Kansas-Nebraska Act called for a new party. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republican-party-united-states">Republican Party</a> was organised that summer and won the presidency in 1860.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1890">1890 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">136 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kaiser Wilhelm II dismisses Bismarck</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After disputes with the young Emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck">Otto von Bismarck</a>'s resignation as Chancellor was accepted. Without him, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s alliances shifted, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s Punch caricatured in 'Dropping the Pilot'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck">Otto von Bismarck</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Einstein submits his general theory of relativity</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">'The Foundation of the General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theory-of-relativity">Theory of Relativity</a>' reached the journal Annalen der Physik. It described gravity as the curvature of spacetime and predicted the bending of light, confirmed in 1919.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Himmler announces the Dachau concentration camp</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>'s police chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-himmler">Heinrich Himmler</a> announced a camp for political prisoners near Dachau, opened two days later. It became the model for the Nazi camp system; over 40,000 died there.</p></div></li></ol>
